# No Dev Server on the Default Branch

Dang runs the dev servers for the main checkouts (`web/`, `agent/`, `studio/`) himself. Before
starting any dev server (`astro dev`, `pnpm dev`, `sanity dev`, etc.), check the branch of the
repo you would start it in:

```bash
git -C <domain-or-worktree> branch --show-current
```

- **`main` or `master`:** don't start it. Assume Dang's server is already running and use it
  (Astro serves `web/` on `http://localhost:4321`, the agent on port 8787). If nothing is
  listening, ask him to start it instead of starting one yourself.
- **Any other branch (a worktree under `<domain>/.worktrees/`):** you may start it, in
  background mode where the app supports it (`astro dev --background`).

`astro dev status` only knows about servers started with `--background`, so it reports "No dev
server is running" even when Dang's foreground server is up. Check the port instead:

```bash
ss -ltnp | rg ':4321|:8787'
```
